   | Terms of Use of Data Hosted By IRSA
   | Terms of Use of Data Hosted by IRSA
   | Terms of Use
   | Public Data
   | Proprietary/Exclusive Access Data
   | Copyrighted Data
   | Acknowledgments & Citations
   | 1. Terms of Use
   | The terms of use depend on whether a data set is public, proprietary /
   | exclusive access, or copyrighted. See the appropriate section below for more
   | information on these three categories.
   | 1.1 Public Data
   | Most data served by IRSA is public, with no usage restrictions.
   | 1.2 Proprietary / Exclusive Access Data
   | Some data sets served by IRSA should only be accessed by persons with
   | explicit rights to the data. Users with data rights can access proprietary or
   | exclusive access data at IRSA after logging in. IRSA systems will not allow
   | previews or downloads of proprietary or exclusive access data for unauthorized
   | users or for authorized users who are not logged in. Questions about
   | authorization to access proprietary or exclusive access data should be directed
   | to the IRSA helpdesk.
   | 1.3 Copyrighted Data
   | Digital Sky Survey data are copyrighted:
   | https://archive.stsci.edu/dss/copyright.html
   | 2. Acknowledgments & Citations
   | It is best practice for users of data hosted at IRSA to include the
   | appropriate acknowledgements and citations in any publications. See
   | https://irsa.ipac.caltech.edu/ack.html
   | for more details.
   | Last updated: 2023-02-08
== IRSA acknowledgement: https://irsa.ipac.caltech.edu/ack.html -> HTTP 200, final URL https://irsa.ipac.caltech.edu/ack.html, 3674 characters
   title: Acknowledging IRSA
   all 26 text lines (first 120 shown)
   | Acknowledging IRSA
   | IRSA Acknowledgement
   | If you use IRSA data or services in your research, please include the
   | appropriate citations, facilities keywords, and acknowledgements in your paper:
   | 1. Include "IRSA" as a facilities keyword if you are submitting to any
   | AAS journal. Also include the facilities keywords corresponding to
   | individual missions used. More information about facilities keywords
   | can be found at http://journals.aas.org/authors/aastex/facility.html
   | Below is a AASTex example for a paper that uses many
   | facilities:
   | \facility {IRSA, Spitzer, WISE, Herschel, Planck,
   | SOFIA, IRTF, IRAS, MSX}
   | 2. Include the following statement in the acknowledgments, in addition
   | to any further acknowledgments required by individual missions and
   | data providers.
   | "This research has made use of the
   | NASA/IPAC Infrared Science Archive, which is funded by the National
   | Aeronautics and Space Administration and operated by the California
   | Institute of Technology."
   | 3. In addition to the above, each data set has its own Digital Object
   | Identifier (DOI) for the specific data set and nearly always has a
   | canonical paper to cite. Please include both of those things in your
   | paper. These can be found on the page corresponding to the data set,
   | e.g., this for
   | MIPSGAL. The service you used may also have its own DOI. A full list of
   | DOIs curated by IPAC can be found here .
